  "clean_text": "Corneal Abrasion: Symptoms, Causes & Treatment | Sankara Corneal Abrasion: Symptoms, Causes & Treatment | Sankara About Services Social Impact Donate Pledge Your Eyes Education Careers Our Blog Contact Services About Us About Pledge Your Eyes Contact Education Social Impact Services Donate Awards Dr.RVR Awards and Biography lasikblr Sankara Lasik Services OUR STORY SERVICES SOCIAL IMPACT Corneal Abrasion: Symptoms, Causes & Treatment Eyecare | 4 MIN READ May 2, 2022 Corneal Abrasion: Symptoms, Causes & Treatment Simply put, corneal abrasion is a scratch on your eye. The scratch can happen in a second or two when dust or dirt gets trapped under your eyelid or when you accidentally poke your eyes. Since the scratch can occur instantly and at any time, it needs to be treated immediately. Let’s understand the condition of corneal abrasion, its symptoms, causes, and treatment. What is Corneal Abrasion? The cornea is the front of the eyes, acting as a protective window. It is the clear part that covers the iris and safeguards the pupil. The cornea plays a crucial role in focusing on the light that allows us to see. Corneal abrasion is a minor scratch or cut on the cornea. A scratched cornea makes your eyes vulnerable to infections and can cause you severe discomfort. What Causes Corneal Abrasion? Any object that comes in direct contact with the front of your eyes is likely to scratch your cornea. Let’s look at more scenarios that can cause corneal abrasion: Poking your eyes with fingers, pen, or even makeup brush. Dust, dirt, ash, or any foreign material that gets trapped in your eyes. Any chemical Using damaged, dirty, or ill-fitted contact lenses Wearing contact lenses while sleeping or for an extended period Rubbing your eyes too hard Playing sports or involve in any high-risk activity without wearing any protective eyewear Signs & Symptoms of a Scratched Cornea The cornea is one of the sensitive parts, and even a minute scratch can be extremely painful and cause a gre..."
